.TH MYGREP 3 "September 2026" "libmyutils 1.0" "libmyutils Manual"
.SH NAME
mygrep \- search a file for lines containing a substring
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "myfilefunctions.h"
.sp
.BI "int mygrep(FILE *" fp ", const char *" search_str ", char ***" matches ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B mygrep()
function scans the open file stream
.I fp
line by line, and collects every line containing
.I search_str
as a substring. A dynamically allocated array of dynamically allocated
strings is returned through
.IR matches .
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of matching lines on success, or \-1 on failure.
The caller is responsible for freeing each string in
.I matches
and then the array itself.
